//! MUST NOT COMPILE.
//!
//! The bug this whole library exists to prevent, in four lines: a verifier
//! written for one fork's layout, pointed at another fork's gindex.
//!
//! Capella's `BeaconState` has 28 fields, so `block_roots` is node 37. Electra
//! added nine fields, which deepened the state tree and moved it to 69. A
//! verifier that checks a Capella state against gindex 69 reads a different
//! node and happily verifies proofs of it -- which is how a runtime pivot
//! (`PIVOT_SLOT`, `PECTRA_FORK_TIMESTAMP`) fails when a fork lands.
//!
//! Here the gindex is a `const fn` of the layout type, so the two cannot be
//! mixed up silently: the number is derived from `Capella`, compared with
//! Electra's, and the build stops with both values printed.

use verife::layout::{block_roots_gindex, Capella}

static_assert(block_roots_gindex<Capella>() == 69)
